## Markdown bold closes before Korean particles

Context:
Graph Chat replies often showed literal `**` around entity names. CommonMark
only closes `**` when the run is right-flanking: after punctuation it must be
followed by whitespace or punctuation. Korean particles attach directly, so
`**[대구지점](/resolve?uri=…)**이` (closer after the link's `)`) and
`**대구지점(E1)**이` stayed unformatted. Reproduced with marked 15.0.12, the
version base.html loads.

Changes:
1. src/front/static/global/js/utils.js
   - New _strongAnyFlankMatch: matches a same-line `**…**` pair at the start
     of the source regardless of flanking. Openers followed by whitespace,
     closers preceded by whitespace, triple runs and multi-line pairs are left
     to the default rules.
   - renderMarkdown installs it once as a marked inline extension
     (strongAnyFlank) that emits standard strong tokens, so every caller
     (Graph Chat, assistant, comments, audit, help) benefits.
2. tests/units/front/test_markdown_strong_any_flank.py
   New node-run tests for the matcher and the one-time marked wiring.
3. tests/units/front/test_frontend_xss_hardening.py
   The renderMarkdown harness extracts single functions, so it now also
   loads the strong-rule helpers it calls.

Modified files:
- src/front/static/global/js/utils.js
- tests/units/front/test_markdown_strong_any_flank.py
- tests/units/front/test_frontend_xss_hardening.py
- changelogs/v0.9.1/simyung-yang_2026-11-02.log

