## Faster Lakebase-backed explorer and chat requests

Context:
Measured on ontobricks-lgit from Korea, an explorer search (preview + expand)
took ~2 s. Server time was 0.30-0.44 s per data request against 0.02-0.09 s for
session-only endpoints, and expansion JSON was sent uncompressed (860 KB, 28 KB
gzipped) across the Pacific. With graph_engine_config.lakebase_branch set (all
demo workspaces), GraphDBFactory built a new BranchLakebaseAuth per request,
so each request created a WorkspaceClient and re-resolved the endpoint host
(and token) over REST before querying (logged on every request).

Changes:
1. src/back/core/databricks/lakebase/BranchLakebaseAuth.py
   New get_branch_lakebase_auth(branch, database): one process-wide instance
   per (branch, database), guarded by a lock, so the resolved host and minted
   JWT (55-minute TTL) survive across requests. Re-exported from the package.
2. src/back/core/graphdb/GraphDBFactory.py
   The explicit-branch path uses get_branch_lakebase_auth, matching the
   bound path's get_lakebase_auth singleton.
3. src/shared/fastapi/main.py
   GZipMiddleware (minimum_size=1024, compresslevel=6). Starlette leaves
   text/event-stream uncompressed, so Graph Chat still streams.
4. tests/units/core/test_branch_lakebase_auth_reuse.py,
   tests/units/core/test_response_compression.py (new)
   Shared instance per key, host resolved once, factory hands stores the same
   auth; gzip registered, large JSON compressed, event streams not.

Modified files:
- src/back/core/databricks/lakebase/BranchLakebaseAuth.py
- src/back/core/databricks/lakebase/__init__.py
- src/back/core/graphdb/GraphDBFactory.py
- src/shared/fastapi/main.py
- tests/units/core/test_branch_lakebase_auth_reuse.py
- tests/units/core/test_response_compression.py
- changelogs/v0.9.1/simyung-yang_2026-11-02.log

