## Bring upstream 0.9.2 fixes for #208, #209 and #210 into integration-latest

Context:
Upstream closed three bugs as "status: Solved". The fixes are on the
databrickslabs/ontobricks 0.9.2 branch only, not on master (master is still
the v0.9.1 merge that integration-latest already contains). 0.9.2 also
carries a version bump, Dependabot lock regeneration and a setup.sh Python
preflight change, so we cherry-picked just the three fix commits instead of
merging the whole branch.
- #208: MCP graph reads were authorised as the MCP app SP, not the end user.
- #209: select_domain did not persist for clients that open a new MCP session
  per tool call (Databricks Playground).
- #210: accepted SPARQL value FILTERs on typed BGPs produced WHERE 1=1.

Changes:
1. Cherry-pick 4823b490 (#208) -> fix(mcp): forward end-user identity past
   the Apps proxy overwrite.
   - MCP sends X-OntoBricks-Acting-Email / -Token next to the M2M bearer;
     PermissionMiddleware trusts them only when the proxy identity equals
     MCP_SP_CLIENT_ID (src/back/core/databricks/ActingIdentity.py,
     src/shared/fastapi/main.py, src/mcp-server/server/http_client.py,
     src/mcp-server/server/session_scope.py).
   - deploy.sh looks up MCP_SP_CLIENT_ID from `databricks apps get`;
     app.yaml.template / scripts/deploy.config.sh carry it; databricks.yml
     adds user_api_scopes (sql, iam.current-user:read,
     iam.access-control:read) to both apps.
   - Conflict: changelogs/v0.9.2/benoitcayladbx_2026-10-30.log
     (modify/delete, file absent here). Kept only the #208 section, dropping
     sections from the two 0.9.2 commits we did not take.
   - src/shared/fastapi/main.py and scripts/deploy.sh auto-merged next to
     our GZip middleware and Lakebase compute step.
2. Cherry-pick 34fc359d (#209) -> fix(mcp): let domain-scoped tools work
   without a sticky session. Domain resolution order: domain_name argument,
   session select_domain, MCP_DEFAULT_DOMAIN, the only published MCP domain
   (src/mcp-server/server/session.py, tools.py, factory.py, docs/mcp.md).
   Applied cleanly.
3. Cherry-pick 80e55609 (#210) -> fix(sparql): compile typed value FILTERs
   into SQL. Filter compilation moved to SparqlValueFilterSql and wired into
   the typed BGP builder; an unmappable validated FILTER now raises
   ValidationError instead of being skipped
   (src/back/core/w3c/sparql/SparqlValueFilterSql.py,
   SparqlTranslator.py). Applied cleanly.

